L808: Appendix 2: Overview of Exercise Training Interventions and Number of Studies per Category
L809: | No. | Intervention | Number of Studies | Description of Interventions |
L810: | --- | --- | --- | --- |
L811: | 1 | Usual training | 16 | Regular taekwondo training as a control condition, general warm-up, including placebo. |
L812: | 2 | Acute Inspiratory Training Group (ARG) | 1 | Inspiratory muscle training (IMT) at 40–50% maximal inspiratory pressure (MIP) for approximately 20 minutes, three times weekly during pre-training warm-up. |
L813: | 3 | Chronic Inspiratory Training Group (CRG) | 1 | IMT at 60–90% MIP with 30 breaths, performed twice daily for 8 weeks. |
L814: | 4 | Conditioning Activity (CA) | 2 | Performing 3 sets of 10 vertical jumps above 40 cm. |
L815: | 5 | Different Area Sizes | 1 | Training sessions conducted in three varied area sizes: 4 × 4 m, 6 × 6 m, and 8 × 8 m. |
L816: | 6 | Double Vibration Foam Rolling (Double VR) | 1 | Six sets of vibration foam rolling specifically targeting the weaker leg. |
L817: | 7 | High-Intensity Interval Training Repeated Sprints (HIITRS) | 1 | Three sets of 10 repetitions of 4-second maximal linear sprints over 5 m, each followed by 28-second walking-based recovery. |
L818: | 8 | High-Intensity Interval Training with Breathing Mask (HIIT-M) | 1 | HIIT performed 3 times weekly for 60–90 minutes, involving short-duration, high-intensity exercises with a breathing mask and 30–60 seconds rest intervals. |
L819: | 9 | High-Intensity Interval Training (HIIT) | 2 | High-intensity exercises at 85–100% HRmax with rest intervals between sets. |
L820: | 10 | High-Intensity Interval Training with Specific Techniques (HIITTS) | 2 | Three rounds of 2-minute sets consisting of 4-second maximal effort kicks followed by 28 seconds of active recovery (1:7 ratio). |
L821: | 11 | Ischemic Preconditioning (IPC) | 1 | Application of pressure at 220 mmHg for preconditioning purposes. |
L822: | 12 | Plyometric Training (PT) | 1 | Three sets of 10 consecutive vertical jumps over a 40 cm obstacle. |
L823: | 13 | Proprioceptive Neuromuscular Facilitation (PNF) | 1 | PNF stretching applied to one leg. |
L824: | 14 | Reducing Training Volume | 1 | Progressive linear reduction of training volume by 3.33% per session, reaching 50% of the original volume at the end of tapering. |
L825: | 15 | Repeated High-Intensity Techniques Training (RTT) | 2 | Three sets of alternating kicks (Bandal-chagui) executed maximally for 5 seconds, with a 10-second rest interval between sets. |
L826: | 16 | Repeated Sprints Training (RST) | 1 | Performing 10 sets of 35 m sprints with 10-second rest intervals. |
L827: | 17 | Resistance Training and Plyometric Training (RT+PT) | 1 | Three half-squats followed immediately by four vertical jumps over a 40 cm barrier. |
L828: | 18 | Resistance Training (RT) | 1 | Three sets of 1 repetition half-squats at 95% 1RM, including deep squat, deadlift, and kettlebell squat jumps. |
L829: | 19 | Vibration Foam Rolling (VR) | 1 | Three sets of foam rolling targeting quadriceps and hamstrings after warm-up. |
L830: Appendix 3: Overview of Nutritional Supplementation Interventions and Number of Studies per Category
L831: | No. | Intervention | Number of Studies | Description of Interventions |
L832: | --- | --- | --- | --- |
L833: | 1 | Usual training | 17 | Regular taekwondo training as a control condition, general warm-up, including placebo. |
L834: | 2 | Caffeine ingestion | 7 | Caffeine supplementation (3.5 mg/kg/day). |
L835: | 3 | Carbohydrate Mouth Rinsing (CMR) | 1 | Mouth rinsing with carbohydrate solution (25 mL, 6.4% maltodextrin) for 15 seconds. |
L836: | 4 | Fufang Ejiaojiang | 1 | Supplementation with 1 tablet daily containing donkey-hide gelatin, Codonopsis pilosula, prepared rehmannia root, red ginseng, maybush, and sucrose. |
L837: | 5 | L-Arginine Supplements (L-ARG) | 1 | Single-dose supplementation of 6 g powdered L-arginine. |
L838: | 6 | Nitrate-Rich Beetroot Juice (BJ) | 1 | Beetroot juice supplementation (400–800 mg of nitrate). |
L839: | 7 | Nitrate and L-Arginine Supplements (NIT+L-ARG) | 1 | Combined supplementation with nitrate (837.40 mg/kg from spinach) and a single dose of 6 g L-arginine powder. |
L840: | 8 | Nitrate Supplements (NIT) | 1 | Nitrate supplementation provided by spinach (837.40 mg/kg). |
L841: | 9 | Nucleotide Formulation (Inmunactive) | 1 | Daily supplementation of 480 mg Inmunactive for 30 days. |
L842: | 10 | Polyphenol Supplementation | 2 | Carob supplementation at a dosage of 40 g/day. |
L843: | 11 | Sodium Bicarbonate Supplementation (NaHCO3) | 1 | Supplementation of 300 mg/kg body mass of sodium bicarbonate. |
L844: | 12 | Vitamin D | 1 | Daily supplementation with one capsule containing 5,000 IU vitamin D3. |
